{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1324","id":5009481113,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUoK9js8AAAABKpadmQ","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/pull/1324","diff_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/pull/1324.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/pull/1324.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/issues/1324","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1324/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1324/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/issues/1324/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/statuses/e5c9c3f2b7bea48f2c7cbbadc9e7de372387c2cd","number":1324,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"T-3109: 1801 Prairie's south stacks dressed, its south bay and south dormer, from HABS photograph 1","user":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4193586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## T-3109 — 1801 Prairie's south face and roof from HABS photograph 1\n\nPiece 3 of T-3003. Worked against Harold Allen's HABS photograph 1 (June 1965) through T-3108's re-solved camera.\n\n**What shipped**\n- **The two south stacks are dressed** with a new, additive `head` on a stone mansard stack in the K01 kit (`k01_frontage_params.py` validates it, `K01.dressed_stack` builds it). Each stack gets a broader base weathered back to the shaft at about 11.85 m, a moulded collar, a diamond-latticed stage (two whole diamonds of crossed raised ribs on each face) and a moulded cap. No other record uses `head`. The other 31 K01/K12/K13/K16 meshes went stale on the generator hash and were re-emitted byte-identical.\n- **Stack heights re-read through the re-solved camera.** The front stack's 18.0 m now fits the print to within about 0.2 m. The rear stack reads 18.5 m, not 20.1 m, so it is lowered and stays hidden from the Taylor eye.\n- **The south canted bay** is built on K08 (`k08.bay.canted` on the kit's `side.north`) to the 1911 sheet's trace: u 13.15→6.87, 0.85 m proud, cants 0.87 m along the wall. It has two storeys and one transomed light per storey on its front. The wall's reconstructed columns behind and beside it (u 11.5 and u 6.5) are removed because the print shows neither. The bay has no cornice of its own: with one light per storey, a K08 moulded cornice pushed its light tier to 0.58 of the full tier, over `check_bay_kit`'s 0.55. The print's cornice over the bay is the main cornice carried round it, which stays open in the match record.\n- **A hooded dormer on the south slope** sits between the stacks with its face at the eave.\n- **Match records:** HABS 1 stays `differs`. Fixed: the stack heads, the stack bases, the bay, the south wall's openings and the dormer. Still open: the SE pinnacle, the recessed range (the sheet steps the wall back to v ≈ 9.8 east of the bay), the light behind the corner balcony, the bay's top and the dormer's slated face (built in stone). Marked within tolerance: the camera foreshortens the south wall about 3× harder than the print does, so the cants are a reading for a camera re-solve. Taylor stays `differs`. 1811's HABS view (it renders 1801 as context) was re-rendered with nothing of 1811 moved and stays `matches`.\n- Liberties L-kimball-1801-stack-heads-3109, -south-dormer-3109 and -south-bay-3109 are added. `liberties.json` and source-use coverage were re-derived.\n\n**Verification (this runner, 4 cores)**\n- Full `check.sh` ran past the 600 s foreground cap here (rc 124 after publish), so the PR's CI gate is the full verdict. These steps ran green locally on the final merged tree: `validate.py --all`, `validate.py --stale`, `image_gate.mjs --check/--test`, `k01_contract.mjs --check/--self-test`, `check_bay_kit.py --check/--self-test`, `check_chimney_kit.py --check/--self-test`, `test_k08_gable`, `test_k01_{pavilion_past_eave,round_corner,side_read_windows,pinnacle_under_block,tower}` and `changelog-entries --check`.\n- Smoke (`--published`): **desktop part 3 PASS** (107 checks) and **mobile part 3 PASS** (107 checks). These are the parts for the building's card and liberties. **Desktop part 1 was cut off by the run's own 590 s timeout** on a loaded box (load 5): 65 checks passed and there were no pageerrors before the kill. It is recorded in dev-smoke-state as the kill it was.\n- Dev was merged in (T-1880, T-1885, T-3155). The liberties were kept from both sides and re-derived, and the 1729 and 1815 meshes were re-emitted byte-identical for the merged generator.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[{"id":12374546158,"node_id":"LA_kwDOUoK9js8AAAAC4ZSW7g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/labels/resume","name":"resume","description":"A run could not finish this; the next one picks it up — reason in the resume: comment","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_